<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ CPI rises 0.6 pct in Sept quarter.</title>
<headline>NZ CPI rises 0.6 pct in Sept quarter.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics New Zealand on Tuesday released the following data on the Consumers Price Index to September 1996:</p>
<p>Quarter-on-quarter percentage changes -</p>
<p>    Sept 1996		   June 1996		  Sept 1995</p>
<p>    +0.6			   +0.8			 +0.2</p>
<p>Year-on-year percentage changes -</p>
<p>    Sept 1996		   June 1996		  Sept 1995</p>
<p>    +2.4			   +2.0			 +3.5</p>
<p>The Reserve Bank of New Zealand in its September Economic Projections forecast CPI inflation at 1.0 percent in the September quarter and 2.9 percent on an annual basis.</p>
<p>Fourteen economists polled by Reuters predicted on average a 0.86 percent quarterly CPI rise, for an annual increase of 2.7 percent.</p>
<p>Excluding credit services the CPI rose 0.4 percent in the quarter and 2.3 percent since the September 1995 quarter.</p>
<p>Contributions of commodity groups to CPI quarterly movements:  </p>
<p>				   Sept 1996	June 1996    Sept 1995</p>
<p>    Food			    0.8		0.9	   -1.3</p>
<p>    Housing			 0.6		1.3	    1.7</p>
<p>    Household operation	-0.1		0.6	    0.3</p>
<p>    Apparel			-0.8		0.8	   -1.1</p>
<p>    Transport		    -0.5		0.2	   -0.1</p>
<p>    Tobacco/Alcohol	     1.3		0.4	    0.9</p>
<p>    Personal &amp; health care    0.4		1.0	    0.4</p>
<p>    Recreation, education     0.6		0.5	    1.1</p>
<p>    Credit services	     3.6		1.0	   -1.1</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom (64 4 4734746)</p>
</text>
